From: John Macias <dencity7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:40:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] mac80211: ath11k/ath12k: backport mac_phy_caps stride
 fix

Backport from ath-next:
7a246c72132e ("wifi: ath11k: fix stride mismatch in mac_phy_caps_parse()")
4c6eb712a91f ("wifi: ath12k: fix stride mismatch in mac_phy_caps_parse()")

When firmware sends MAC/PHY capability TLVs shorter than the driver's
struct, both parsers size the buffer by the clamped TLV length but
advance the copy destination by the full struct size, so the second and
later entries are written past the end of the allocation
(CVE-2026-90398 / CVE-2026-90399). backports-7.2 still has the old code.

Both patches apply to backports-7.2 on top of the current mac80211
patch set with offsets only. Compile tested: ath11k for qualcommax/ipq807x
and ath12k for qualcommbe/ipq53xx with the OpenWrt toolchain, no new
warnings.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: John Macias <dencity7@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/26175
Signed-off-by: Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5062c68dfdee8eef1f1ba14f75ed4ff3444280c5)
